// orange graffiti wall, so it was first unwarped to a square (the paper's four corners, a homography; the wall and the grey strip at the paper's left are dropped), its uneven background removed, its luminance lightly
// blurred and cut at five levels (marching squares), and every contour simplified (about a pixel). The gold glitter (the lit windows, by hue) and the silver glitter (the hatched blocks beside the maze, a zone) were
// segmented apart from the white paint and taken out of the tones, and each got its own contours: its outline and its brighter facets. Each group is a list of closed loops, nested ones are holes (even-odd), in
// rectified cover pixels (the paper is 1000 square), as half-pixel integers: "n x0 y0 dx dy dx dy …", every number a variable-length code of 5 bits per character (the characters A-Z a-z 0-9 + - : 0-31 end a number,
// 32-63 continue it), deltas zig-zagged. Decoded by saDecode(): [{ l: group, pts: [[x, y] …], a: area }].
